---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import Weather from '../components/Weather.astro';
import AskeatonLandmarks from '../components/AskeatonLandmarks.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="My Place"
	description="A look at Askeaton, Co. Limerick, and the places that shape everyday life in my hometown."
	pubDate={new Date('September 23 2026')}
	heroImageSrc="/images/askeaton/myplace.png"
	heroImageAlt="Aerial view of Askeaton, County Limerick"
	heroTitle="My Place"
	heroSubtitle="Askeaton, Co. Limerick — a close-knit town shaped by history, community and the Shannon estuary."
>
	<p>
		Askeaton is a small town in County Limerick that sits on the edge of the Shannon estuary. It is
		one of those places where the pace is a little slower, the landscape is always changing, and the
		history feels close to the surface.
	</p>

	<p>
		For me, it is a place shaped by old stone buildings, a strong sense of community, and the quiet
		beauty of the west of Ireland. Whether walking past the castle, heading through the town centre,
		or looking out over the surrounding countryside, it is easy to see why Askeaton feels like home.
	</p>

	<p>
		The town has a mix of heritage and everyday life, with the Franciscan Friary, the church, the
		local leisure centre, and the river all giving the place its own character. It is a place of both
		memory and movement, where history sits comfortably alongside modern community life.
	</p>

	<AskeatonLandmarks />
	<Weather />
</Layout>
